# Shokunin routing

This repo always uses the curated Shokunin set in `.cursor/skills/`. Cursor loads those folders automatically. Before doing the work in the left column, read that skill's `SKILL.md` and follow it.

| Work | Skill |
| --- | --- |
| Game definition, moves, phases, Local/SocketIO, playerView | `boardgame-io` (always for this project) |
| Table, HUD, card, or layout UI | `component-forge` |
| Reveal, collapse, or other motion | `motion-craft` |
| Design critique or polish | `impeccable` |
| Visual identity (restrained cyberpunk) | `taste` |
| Pattern / UX inventory | `ui-ux-pro-max` |
| Interaction timing and easing | `emil-design-eng` |
| Layout across viewports | `responsive-engine` |
| Vitest or rules-engine tests | `test-commander` |
| Browser verification | `playwright` |
| Review of a change | `code-review` or `comprehensive-review` |
| Three.js / render cost | `performance-profiler` |
| Failure paths and logging | `error-handler` |
| Multi-step implementation | `plan` |
| Product or rules docs | `documentation` |
| Git history or PR shape | `git-workflow` |
| Auth, matchmaking, or sockets | `auth-architect` then `api-forge` |
| Client/server trust boundary | `web-security` |
| YouTube transcript, search, channel, or playlist | `youtube-full` |
| YouTube visual timeline / watch on screen | `youtube-watch` |

Do not load kubernetes, docker, flutter, finance, kami, or windows-powershell. If a needed skill is missing, use `find-skills`.

0uroboros copy rules still win: sentence case, no em dashes, accents only for state meaning.
